 "method": "Owl retune of the v1 pipeline: STFT (4096-pt Hann, 256 hop -> 10.8 Hz bins, 5.8 ms steps) dominant-peak pitch track in 150-900 Hz; hoot segmentation on the 150-900 Hz band Hilbert envelope (5 ms smoothing): body pass onset -12 dB / offset -17 dB rel. file peak, min off-time 60 ms, min hoot 120 ms; sensitive pass onset -16 / offset -21 dB, extras kept only if non-overlapping with body hoots and spectral-peak prominence >= 8 dB. The thresholds were set from this file's measured in-band floor (envelope median -30 dB, p95 -25 dB between series; hoot peaks p95 -2 dB) \u2014 the v1 cardinal thresholds (-24/-31 dB) sit inside this floor and never close, which is why the first pass fused the whole file into one span. Within each hoot, pitch/harmonic statistics use only frames whose band envelope is >= -22 dB, because the quiet floor is broad low-frequency noise wandering 200-290 Hz and unmasked edge frames track it instead of the hoot. Per hoot: f_start/f_end = median track over first/last 20% of kept frames, f_med = whole hoot, f_peak/f_min = 95th/5th percentile; harm2/harm3 = median frame ratio of the STFT magnitude at 2f0 / 3f0 to the fundamental; peak_amp_rel = max of the band envelope (linear, file peak-normalized). Contour and amplitude templates = per-hoot tracks resampled to 16 normalized points, median across instances of the position. Series = hoot groups split at gaps > 3.0 s; positions numbered from 1 within each series. Contamination scan (v2 battery): short-time RMS in 0.25 s windows for the 40-500 Hz band and full band; a swell = 1 s-smoothed level > file median + 7 dB sustained >= 1.5 s (spans < 2 s apart merged).",
